course: dictionary
lesson: 15216
title: Sentimental: feelings, memories or too much?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «She looked at the faded photo and felt sentimental about the summer at the lake.» The photo is old and faded, and she is thinking about the past. Sentimental means full of tender feelings, like love, sadness or longing, especially about times gone by.
explain: «The old teddy is worth only two pounds, but it has sentimental value.» Only two pounds means money is not the point. The teddy is precious because of the memories it brings. Sentimental value means something you keep for its memories, not for what it would sell for.
explain: «The film was so sentimental and sugary that it felt fake.» Here the word is a criticism. Sugary and fake show the feelings are overdone and not real. The same word can be warm praise or harsh criticism, so always check the clues around it.
fact: Sentimental means full of tender feelings, such as love, sadness or longing.
fact: A sentimental person is easily moved, especially when thinking about the past.
fact: «Sentimental value» means a thing is kept for its memories, not for its money.
fact: When a critic calls something sentimental, they mean it is too soft and sugary, and it seems overdone or not real.
fact: To check the meaning, swap in a word like «emotional» for warm praise, or «soppy» for criticism, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «He found his old school jumper and felt sentimental about his first year.» What does sentimental mean here? | Very fast | *Full of tender feelings about the past | Too small to wear | Angry at the cold weather
exercise: «The broken watch was worth nothing in money, but it had great sentimental value.» What does sentimental value mean? | *It is kept for the memories it brings, not for money | It can still tell the time perfectly | It was bought in a big sale | It is made of real gold
exercise: Mia says, «That ending was far too sentimental, so sugary it felt fake.» What is Mia criticising? | The colours were too bright | The price was too high | The ending was too short | *Feelings that are soft, sugary and overdone
test: «My gran gets sentimental every time we sing that old song.» What does gets sentimental suggest? | Gets sleepy and yawns | Gets lost on the way home | *Gets emotional, thinking tenderly of the past | Gets angry and shouts at the radio
test: Which thing is most likely to have sentimental value? | A shiny car sold for a fortune | *A faded birthday card from your nan | A new coin that is worth a lot of money | A bag of sweets bought yesterday
exam: Ben says, «The advert is too sentimental.» What is he criticising? | Its short length | *Feelings that are soft, sugary and overdone | Its high price | Its bright colours
